          "processed"
        ],
        "type": "string"
      },
      "mandate_import_links": {
        "type": "object",
        "title": "MandateImportLinks",
        "description": "Related resources",
        "properties": {
          "creditor": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "ID of the associated creditor.",
            "example": "CR123"
          }
        }
      },
      "mandate_import_single_resource_response": {
        "type": "object",
        "title": "MandateImportSingleResourceResponse",
        "description": "",
        "properties": {
          "mandate_imports": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "Mandate Imports allow you to migrate existing mandates from other providers into the\nGoCardless platform.\n\nThe process is as follows:\n\n  1. [Create a mandate import](#mandate-imports-create-a-new-mandate-import)\n  2. [Add entries](#mandate-import-entries-add-a-mandate-import-entry) to the import\n  3. [Submit](#mandate-imports-submit-a-mandate-import) the import\n  4. Wait until a member of the GoCardless team approves the import, at which point the mandates will be created\n  5. [Link up the mandates](#mandate-import-entries-list-all-mandate-import-entries) in your system\n\nWhen you add entries to your mandate import, they are not turned into actual mandates\nuntil the mandate import is submitted by you via the API, and then processed by a member\nof the GoCardless team. When that happens, a mandate will be created for each entry in the import.\n\nWe will issue a `mandate_created` webhook for each entry, which will be the same as the webhooks\ntriggered when [ creating a mandate ](#mandates-create-a-mandate) using the mandates API. Once these\nwebhooks start arriving, any reconciliation can now be accomplished by\n[checking the current status](#mandate-imports-get-a-mandate-import) of the mandate import and\n[linking up the mandates to your system](#mandate-import-entries-list-all-mandate-import-entries).\n\n<p class=\"notice\">Note that all Mandate Imports have an upper limit of 30,000 entries, so we recommend you split your import into several smaller imports if you're planning to exceed this threshold.</p>\n\n<p class=\"restricted-notice\"><strong>Restricted</strong>: This API is currently only available for approved integrators - please <a href=\"mailto:help@gocardless.com\">get in touch</a> if you would like to use this API.</p>",
            "properties": {
              "id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Unique identifier, beginning with \"IM\".",
                "example": "IM123"
              },
              "created_at": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Fixed [timestamp](#api-usage-dates-and-times), recording when this resource was created.",
                "example": "2014-01-01T12:00:00.000Z",
                "format": "date-time"
              },
              "status": {
                "description": "The status of the mandate import.\n\n- `created`: A new mandate import.\n- `submitted`: After the integrator has finished adding mandates and [submitted](#mandate-imports-submit-a-mandate-import) the import.\n- `cancelled`: If the integrator [cancelled](#mandate-imports-cancel-a-mandate-import) the mandate import.\n- `processing`: Once a mandate import has been approved by a GoCardless team member it will be in this state while mandates are imported.\n- `processed`: When all mandates have been imported successfully.",
                "example": "created",
                "enum": [
                  "created",
                  "submitted",
                  "cancelled",
                  "processing",
                  "processed"
                ],
                "type": "string"
              },
              "scheme": {
                "description": "The scheme of the mandates to be imported.<br>All mandates in a single mandate\nimport must be for the same scheme.",
                "example": "bacs",
                "enum": [
                  "ach",
                  "autogiro",
                  "bacs",
                  "becs",
                  "becs_nz",
                  "betalingsservice",
                  "faster_payments",
                  "pad",
                  "pay_to",
                  "sepa_core"
                ],
                "type": "string"
              },
              "links": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Related resources",
                "properties": {
                  "creditor": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "ID of the associated creditor.",
                    "example": "CR123"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "mandate_import_entry": {
        "type": "object",
        "title": "Mandate Import Entries",
        "description": "Mandate Import Entries are added to a [Mandate Import](#core-endpoints-mandate-imports).\nEach entry corresponds to one mandate to be imported into GoCardless.\n\nTo import a mandate you will need:\n<ol>\n  <li>Identifying information about the customer (name/company and address)</li>\n  <li>Bank account details, consisting of an account holder name and\n     either an IBAN or <a href=\"#appendix-local-bank-details\">local bank details</a></li>\n  <li>Amendment details (SEPA only)</li>\n</ol>\n\nWe suggest you provide a `record_identifier` (which is unique within the context of a\nsingle mandate import) to help you to identify mandates that have been created once the\nimport has been processed by GoCardless. You can\n[list the mandate import entries](#mandate-import-entries-list-all-mandate-import-entries),\nmatch them up in your system using the `record_identifier`, and look at the `links`\nfields to find the mandate, customer and customer bank account that have been imported.\n\n<p class=\"restricted-notice\"><strong>Restricted</strong>: This API is currently only available for approved integrators - please <a href=\"mailto:help@gocardless.com\">get in touch</a> if you would like to use this API.</p>",
        "properties": {
          "record_identifier": {
            "type": "string",
            "nullable": true,
            "description": "A unique identifier for this entry, which you can use (once the import has been\nprocessed by GoCardless) to identify the records that have been created. Limited\nto 255 characters.\n",
            "example": "bank-file.xml/line-1"
          },
          "created_at": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Fixed [timestamp](#api-usage-dates-and-times), recording when this resource was created.",
            "example": "2014-01-01T12:00:00.000Z",
            "format": "date-time"
          },
          "links": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "Related resources",
            "properties": {
              "mandate_import": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "The ID of the mandate import. This is returned when you\n[create a Mandate Import](#mandate-imports-create-a-new-mandate-import).\n",
                "example": "IM0000AAAAAAA"
              },
              "mandate": {
                "allOf": [
                  {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/mandate"
                  },
                  {
                    "description": "The ID of the mandate which was created when the mandate import was processed."
                  }
                ]
              },
              "customer": {
                "allOf": [
                  {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/customer"
                  },
                  {
                    "description": "The ID of the customer which was created when the mandate import was processed."
                  }
                ]
              },
              "customer_bank_account": {
                "allOf": [
                  {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/customer_bank_account"
                  },
                  {
                    "description": "The ID of the customer bank account which was created when the mandate import\nwas processed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          },
          "processing_errors": {
            "type": "object",
            "nullable": true,
            "description": "Per-resource processing errors"
          }
        }
      },
      "mandate_import_entry_record_identifier": {
        "type": "string",
        "nullable": true,
        "title": "MandateImportEntryRecordIdentifier",
        "description": "A unique identifier for this entry, which you can use (once the import has been\nprocessed by GoCardless) to identify the records that have been created. Limited\nto 255 characters.\n",
        "example": "bank-file.xml/line-1"
      },
      "mandate_import_entry_mandate_import": {
        "type": "string",
        "title": "MandateImportEntryMandateImport",
        "description": "The ID of the mandate import. This is returned when you\n[create a Mandate Import](#mandate-imports-create-a-new-mandate-import).\n",
        "example": "IM0000AAAAAAA"
      },
      "mandate_import_entry_links": {
        "type": "object",
        "title": "MandateImportEntryLinks",
        "description": "Related resources",
        "properties": {
          "mandate_import": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The ID of the mandate import. This is returned when you\n[create a Mandate Import](#mandate-imports-create-a-new-mandate-import).\n",
            "example": "IM0000AAAAAAA"
          },
          "mandate": {
            "allOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/mandate"
              },
              {
                "description": "The ID of the mandate which was created when the mandate import was processed."
              }
            ]
          },
          "customer": {
            "allOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/customer"
              },
              {
                "description": "The ID of the customer which was created when the mandate import was processed."
              }
            ]
          },
          "customer_bank_account": {
            "allOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/customer_bank_account"
              },
              {
                "description": "The ID of the customer bank account which was created when the mandate import\nwas processed."
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "mandate_import_entry_status": {
        "title": "MandateImportEntryStatus",
        "description": "One of:\n\n- `successfully_processed`: the entry has been imported and the associated records created.\n- `unsuccessfully_processed`: the entry could not be processed due to an error, see the 'processing_errors' value",
        "example": "successfully_processed",
        "enum": [
          "successfully_processed",
          "unsuccessfully_processed"
        ],
        "type": "string"
      },
      "mandate_import_entry_processing_errors": {
        "type": "object",
        "nullable": true,
        "title": "MandateImportEntryProcessingErrors",
        "description": "Per-resource processing errors"
      },
