            "example": "BR123"
          }
        }
      },
      "redirect_flow_single_resource_response": {
        "type": "object",
        "title": "RedirectFlowSingleResourceResponse",
        "description": "",
        "properties": {
          "redirect_flows": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "<p class=\"deprecated-notice\"><strong>Deprecated</strong>: Redirect Flows are legacy APIs and cannot be used by new integrators.\n    The <a href=\"https://developer.gocardless.com/api-reference/#billing-requests-billing-requests\">Billing Request flow</a> API should be used for your payment flows.</p>\n\nRedirect flows enable you to use GoCardless' [hosted payment pages](https://pay-sandbox.gocardless.com/AL000000AKFPFF) to set up mandates with your customers. These pages are fully compliant and have been translated into Danish, Dutch, French, German, Italian, Norwegian, Portuguese, Slovak, Spanish and Swedish.\n\nThe overall flow is:\n\n1. You [create](#redirect-flows-create-a-redirect-flow) a redirect flow for your customer, and redirect them to the returned redirect url, e.g. `https://pay.gocardless.com/flow/RE123`.\n\n2. Your customer supplies their name, email, address, and bank account details, and submits the form. This securely stores their details, and redirects them back to your `success_redirect_url` with `redirect_flow_id=RE123` in the querystring.\n\n3. You [complete](#redirect-flows-complete-a-redirect-flow) the redirect flow, which creates a [customer](#core-endpoints-customers), [customer bank account](#core-endpoints-customer-bank-accounts), and [mandate](#core-endpoints-mandates), and returns the ID of the mandate. You may wish to create a [subscription](#core-endpoints-subscriptions) or [payment](#core-endpoints-payments) at this point.\n\nOnce you have [completed](#redirect-flows-complete-a-redirect-flow) the redirect flow via the API, you should display a confirmation page to your customer, confirming that their Direct Debit has been set up. You can build your own page, or redirect to the one we provide in the `confirmation_url` attribute of the redirect flow.\n\nRedirect flows expire 30 minutes after they are first created. You cannot complete an expired redirect flow. For an integrator this is shorter and they will expire after 10 minutes.",
            "properties": {
              "id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Unique identifier, beginning with \"RE\".",
                "example": "RE123456"
              },
              "description": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "A description of the item the customer is paying for. This will be shown on the hosted payment pages.",
                "example": "Standard subscription"
              },
              "session_token": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "The customer's session ID must be provided when the redirect flow is set up and again when it is completed. This allows integrators to ensure that the user who was originally sent to the GoCardless payment pages is the one who has completed them.",
                "example": "SESS_wSs0uGYMISxzqOBq"
              },
              "scheme": {
                "description": "The Direct Debit scheme of the mandate. If specified, the payment pages will only allow the set-up of a mandate for the specified scheme. It is recommended that you leave this blank so the most appropriate scheme is picked based on the customer's bank account.",
                "example": "bacs",
                "enum": [
                  "ach",
                  "autogiro",
                  "bacs",
                  "becs",
                  "becs_nz",
                  "betalingsservice",
                  "pad",
                  "sepa_core"
                ],
                "nullable": true,
                "type": "string"
              },
              "success_redirect_url": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "The URL to redirect to upon successful mandate setup. You must use a URL beginning `https` in the live environment.",
                "example": "https://example.com/pay/confirm"
              },
              "confirmation_url": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "The URL of a confirmation page, which you may optionally redirect the customer to rather than use your own page, that confirms in their chosen language that their Direct Debit has been set up successfully. Only returned once the customer has set up their mandate via the payment pages and the redirect flow has been [completed](#redirect-flows-complete-a-redirect-flow), and only available for 15 minutes from when you complete the redirect flow. The structure of this URL may change at any time, so you should read it directly from the API response.",
                "example": "https://pay.gocardless.com/flow/RE123/success"
              },
              "redirect_url": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "The URL of the hosted payment pages for this redirect flow. This is the URL you should redirect your customer to.",
                "example": "http://pay.gocardless.com/flow/RE123"
              },
              "created_at": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Fixed [timestamp](#api-usage-dates-and-times), recording when this resource was created.",
                "example": "2014-01-01T12:00:00.000Z",
                "format": "date-time"
              },
              "links": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "",
                "properties": {
                  "creditor": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "The [creditor](#core-endpoints-creditors) for whom the mandate will be created. The `name` of the creditor will be displayed on the payment page.",
                    "example": "CR123"
                  },
                  "mandate": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "ID of [mandate](#core-endpoints-mandates) created by this redirect flow.<br/>**Note**: this property will not be present until the redirect flow has been successfully completed.",
                    "example": "MD123"
                  },
                  "customer": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "ID of [customer](#core-endpoints-customers) created by this redirect flow.<br/>**Note**: this property will not be present until the redirect flow has been successfully completed.",
                    "example": "CU123"
                  },
                  "customer_bank_account": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "ID of [customer bank account](#core-endpoints-customer-bank-accounts) created by this redirect flow.<br/>**Note**: this property will not be present until the redirect flow has been successfully completed.",
                    "example": "BA123"
                  },
                  "billing_request": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "ID of [billing request](#billing-requests-billing-requests) that a redirect flow can create.<br />**Note**: The redirect flow will only create a billing request in the event the redirect flow is eligible to send the payer down this new and improved flow",
                    "example": "BR123"
                  }
                }
              },
              "metadata": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Key-value store of custom data. Up to 3 keys are permitted, with key names up to 50 characters and values up to 500 characters. _Note:_ This should not be used for storing PII data.",
                "example": {
                  "salesforce_id": "ABCD1234"
                }
              },
              "mandate_reference": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Mandate reference generated by GoCardless or submitted by an integrator."
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "refund": {
        "type": "object",
        "title": "Refunds",
        "description": "Refund objects represent (partial) refunds of a [payment](#core-endpoints-payments) back to the [customer](#core-endpoints-customers).\n\nGoCardless will notify you via a [webhook](#appendix-webhooks) whenever a refund is created, and will update the `amount_refunded` property of the payment.",
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Unique identifier, beginning with \"RF\".",
            "example": "RF123"
          },
          "created_at": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Fixed [timestamp](#api-usage-dates-and-times), recording when this resource was created.",
            "example": "2014-01-01T12:00:00.000Z",
            "format": "date-time"
          },
          "amount": {
            "oneOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "integer"
              }
            ],
            "description": "Amount in minor unit (e.g. pence in GBP, cents in EUR).",
            "example": 150
          },
          "currency": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "[ISO 4217](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_4217#Active_codes) currency code. This is set to the currency of the refund's [payment](#core-endpoints-payments).",
            "example": "EUR"
          },
          "status": {
            "description": "One of:\n\n- `created`: the refund has been created\n- `pending_submission`: the refund has been created, but not yet submitted to the banks\n- `submitted`: the refund has been submitted to the banks\n- `paid`:  the refund has been included in a [payout](#core-endpoints-payouts)\n- `cancelled`: the refund has been cancelled\n- `bounced`: the refund has failed to be paid\n- `funds_returned`: the refund has had its funds returned",
            "example": "submitted",
            "enum": [
              "created",
              "pending_submission",
              "submitted",
              "paid",
              "cancelled",
              "bounced",
              "funds_returned"
            ],
            "type": "string"
          },
          "reference": {
            "type": "string",
            "nullable": true,
            "description": "An optional reference that will appear on your customer's bank statement. The character limit for this reference is dependent on the scheme.<br /> <strong>ACH</strong> - 10 characters<br /> <strong>Autogiro</strong> - 11 characters<br /> <strong>Bacs</strong> - 10 characters<br /> <strong>BECS</strong> - 30 characters<br /> <strong>BECS NZ</strong> - 12 characters<br /> <strong>Betalingsservice</strong> - 30 characters<br /> <strong>Faster Payments</strong> - 18 characters<br /> <strong>PAD</strong> - scheme doesn't offer references<br /> <strong>PayTo</strong> - 18 characters<br /> <strong>SEPA</strong> - 140 characters<br /> Note that this reference must be unique (for each merchant) for the BECS scheme as it is a scheme requirement. <p class='restricted-notice'><strong>Restricted</strong>: You can only specify a payment reference for Bacs payments (that is, when collecting from the UK) if you're on the <a href='https://gocardless.com/pricing'>GoCardless Plus, Pro or Enterprise packages</a>.</p> <p class='restricted-notice'><strong>Restricted</strong>: You can not specify a payment reference for Faster Payments.</p>",
            "example": "WINEBOX001"
          },
          "metadata": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "Key-value store of custom data. Up to 3 keys are permitted, with key names up to 50 characters and values up to 500 characters."
          },
          "links": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "",
            "properties": {
              "payment": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "ID of the [payment](#core-endpoints-payments) against which the refund is being made.",
                "example": "PM123"
              },
              "mandate": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "ID of the [mandate](#core-endpoints-mandates) against which the refund is being made.",
                "example": "MD123"
              }
            }
          },
          "fx": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "",
            "properties": {
              "exchange_rate": {
                "type": "string",
                "nullable": true,
                "description": "Rate used in the foreign exchange of the `amount` into the `fx_currency`.\nPresent only after a resource is paid out. Has up to 10 decimal places.",
                "example": "1.1234567890"
              },
              "estimated_exchange_rate": {
                "type": "string",
                "nullable": true,
                "description": "Estimated rate that will be used in the foreign exchange of the `amount` into the `fx_currency`.\nThis will vary based on the prevailing market rate until the moment that it is paid out.\nPresent only before a resource is paid out. Has up to 10 decimal places.",
                "example": "1.1234567890"
              },
              "fx_amount": {
                "oneOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "string",
                    "nullable": true
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "integer"
                  }
                ],
                "description": "Amount that was paid out in the `fx_currency` after foreign exchange.\nPresent only after the resource has been paid out.",
                "example": 1150
              },
              "fx_currency": {
                "description": "[ISO 4217](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_4217#Active_codes) code for the currency in which amounts will be paid out (after foreign exchange). Currently \"AUD\", \"CAD\", \"DKK\", \"EUR\", \"GBP\", \"NZD\", \"SEK\" and \"USD\" are supported. Present only if payouts will be (or were) made via foreign exchange.",
                "example": "EUR",
                "enum": [
                  "AUD",
                  "CAD",
                  "DKK",
                  "EUR",
                  "GBP",
                  "NZD",
                  "SEK",
                  "USD"
                ],
                "nullable": true,
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "refund_id": {
        "type": "string",
        "title": "RefundId",
        "description": "Unique identifier, beginning with \"RF\".",
        "example": "RF123"
      },
      "refund_identity": {
        "type": "string",
        "title": "RefundIdentity",
        "description": "Unique identifier, beginning with \"RF\".",
        "example": "RF123"
      },
      "refund_created_at": {
        "type": "string",
        "title": "RefundCreatedAt",
        "description": "Fixed [timestamp](#api-usage-dates-and-times), recording when this resource was created.",
        "example": "2014-01-01T12:00:00.000Z",
        "format": "date-time"
      },
      "refund_currency": {
        "type": "string",
        "title": "RefundCurrency",
        "description": "[ISO 4217](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_4217#Active_codes) currency code. This is set to the currency of the refund's [payment](#core-endpoints-payments).",
        "example": "EUR"
      },
      "refund_status": {
        "title": "RefundStatus",
        "description": "One of:\n\n- `created`: the refund has been created\n- `pending_submission`: the refund has been created, but not yet submitted to the banks\n- `submitted`: the refund has been submitted to the banks\n- `paid`:  the refund has been included in a [payout](#core-endpoints-payouts)\n- `cancelled`: the refund has been cancelled\n- `bounced`: the refund has failed to be paid\n- `funds_returned`: the refund has had its funds returned",
        "example": "submitted",
        "enum": [
          "created",
          "pending_submission",
          "submitted",
          "paid",
          "cancelled",
          "bounced",
          "funds_returned"
        ],
        "type": "string"
      },
      "refund_reference": {
        "type": "string",
        "nullable": true,
        "title": "RefundReference",
        "description": "An optional reference that will appear on your customer's bank statement. The character limit for this reference is dependent on the scheme.<br /> <strong>ACH</strong> - 10 characters<br /> <strong>Autogiro</strong> - 11 characters<br /> <strong>Bacs</strong> - 10 characters<br /> <strong>BECS</strong> - 30 characters<br /> <strong>BECS NZ</strong> - 12 characters<br /> <strong>Betalingsservice</strong> - 30 characters<br /> <strong>Faster Payments</strong> - 18 characters<br /> <strong>PAD</strong> - scheme doesn't offer references<br /> <strong>PayTo</strong> - 18 characters<br /> <strong>SEPA</strong> - 140 characters<br /> Note that this reference must be unique (for each merchant) for the BECS scheme as it is a scheme requirement. <p class='restricted-notice'><strong>Restricted</strong>: You can only specify a payment reference for Bacs payments (that is, when collecting from the UK) if you're on the <a href='https://gocardless.com/pricing'>GoCardless Plus, Pro or Enterprise packages</a>.</p> <p class='restricted-notice'><strong>Restricted</strong>: You can not specify a payment reference for Faster Payments.</p>",
        "example": "WINEBOX001"
      },
      "refund_amount": {
        "oneOf": [
          {
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "type": "integer"
          }
        ],
        "title": "RefundAmount",
        "description": "Amount in minor unit (e.g. pence in GBP, cents in EUR).",
        "example": 150
      },
      "refund_total_amount_confirmation": {
        "oneOf": [
          {
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "type": "integer"
          }
        ],
        "title": "RefundTotalAmountConfirmation",
        "description": "Total expected refunded amount in minor unit (e.g. pence/cents/öre). If there are\nother partial refunds against this payment, this value should be the sum of the\nexisting refunds plus the amount of the refund being created.\n<br />\nMust be supplied if `links[payment]` is present.\n<p class=\"notice\">It is possible to opt out of requiring <code>total_amount_confirmation</code>, please contact <a href=\"mailto:support@gocardless.com\">our support team</a> for more information.</p>",
        "example": "150"
      },
      "refund_fx": {
        "type": "object",
        "title": "RefundFx",
        "description": "",
        "properties": {
          "exchange_rate": {
            "type": "string",
            "nullable": true,
            "description": "Rate used in the foreign exchange of the `amount` into the `fx_currency`.\nPresent only after a resource is paid out. Has up to 10 decimal places.",
            "example": "1.1234567890"
          },
